1. The Regent in implementing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women as referred to in Article 9 shall undertake efforts to:
a. coordinate implementation among Regional Apparatus;
b. cooperate with the central government, provincial government, and other regency/city governments in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
c. strengthen the capacity of Gender institutions;
d. facilitate services for the Protection of Women;
e. provide services for the Protection of Women;
f. implement affirmative action for the Protection of Women; and
g. prepare a data system for the Protection of Women including a data system for Violence Against Women.
2. The implementation of policies, programs, and activities as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be coordinated by the Vice Regent.

I. GENERAL

The position, role and quality of women in current developments have undergone changes in efforts to realize gender equality and justice, both in family life, society, nation and state. Protection of human rights has also become a spotlight, especially regarding all forms of violence against women which constitute violations of human rights, so that women need to be protected in their dignity and honor and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination.

In order to protect the community, realize equity, and justice as an obligation of the regional government to provide protection and welfare for women, the Government of Bandung Regency stipulates a Regional Regulation on Women's Protection. The implementation of women's protection is carried out based on the principles of Pancasila and grounded in the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia, which includes:
a. Protection;
b. Respect for human rights;
c. Gender justice and equality;
d. Non-discrimination; and
e. Best interests of women.

The objectives of establishing the Regional Regulation on Women's Protection are:
a. To ensure the fulfillment of women's rights so they can live and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and honor;
b. To provide gender justice and equality;
c. To provide protection and security for women victims of violence and discrimination, as well as criminal acts of trafficking in persons;
d. To eliminate all forms of violence and discrimination against women;
e. To provide services to women victims of violence and witnesses;
f. To provide recovery for women victims of violence.

